— A PERSONAL NOTE— 307
parisons be别 "this" and "that," are meaningless within the cre-
ative experience.
It is what it is.
³ is a "dream factory," a town of talkers. Go to any of
the е hangouts around town and you'll hear people μ
about the scripts they're going to ・e, the movies they're going to
produce, the щ they're going to make.
It's all talk.
Action is יter, right? What a person does, and not what he
says, is who he is.
Everybody's a ・er.
There is a tendency in ³ to second-guess the ・er;
the studio, the star, the director, the producer will all make changes
in the script that they think will "improve" it. Sometimes they do,
and sometimes they don't. Most people in ³ assume
they're "セ" than the original material. "They" know what has to
be done to "make it better." Directors do this all the time.
A film director can take a great script and make a great film. Or
he can take a great script and make a terrible film. But he can't take
a terrible script and make a great film.
No way.
Some film あ know how to improve a  by visu-
ally tightening the story line. They can take a wordy ¦ scene
of three to four pages and condense it into a ि and 
three-minute scene that "works" with five lines of ¦, three
