of the script.
That's the exception, not the rule.
The rule is that most あ and stars in ³ have little
or no story sense at all. They'll second-guess the ・er, making
changes in the story line that weaken and distort it, and eventually a
lot of money is spent making a lousy film that 友 Í to see.
And you're only as good as your last film.

308 —¡ —
In the long run, of course, ח loses—the studios lose
